on-arrival: lsr_split = 1;

= The Extraordinary Party Congress

In the first half of December the party met in Petrograd in an extraordinary congress. The question was the party's attitude to the Bolshevik takeover: whether it was, in some sense, a historical development, to be criticised but not fought; or a conspiracy, a betrayal of the revolution, to be resisted by every means.

Martov's Internationalists, with the support of the provincial delegates, argue for the first. Potresov, Tsereteli's circle and the Right Defencists argue for the second. [? if bol_regime = 0 : The Bolsheviks are no longer a threat, and the question is more theoretical: what is the party's attitude to the Soviet parties that govern? ?]

The Left SRs held their own founding congress on the same days, with 116 delegates from 99 organisations.

- @martov: Adopt Martov's line.
- @defencist: Adopt the Defencist line.
- @balance: Try to hold both sides together.

@martov
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 14, -12);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -10, 12);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -4, 15);
Q.war_line -= 2;
Q.martov_line = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 3, rel_lsr: 3});
!}

Martov's line won, narrowly. The Defencists resigned from the Central Committee. The party has a new leadership, and fewer friends on the Right.

@defencist
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 8, -6);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 4, -6);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -8, 20);
Q.war_line += 1;
Q.martov_line = 0;
Q.members -= 8;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -4, rel_kad: 3});
!}

The Defencists carried the day, and a number of Internationalist circles left the party.

@balance
on-arrival: {!
for (var f of Q.factions) { RO.fac(Q, f, 0, 4); }
Q.martov_line = 0;
!}

A compromise resolution was adopted. Nobody is satisfied, but nobody resigned.
